{
  "name": "Daily outreach drafts from Google Maps with Apify, Google Sheets and Gmail (never sends)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Daily outreach drafts: Google Maps → role inbox → Sheet → Gmail drafts (never sent)\n\nEvery weekday morning this workflow finds new local businesses for one of your searches (for example \"event agency in Manchester\"; a different search × city pair each weekday), finds the inbox they publish on their own website, logs them in a Google Sheet and leaves one Gmail **draft** per company. It never sends an email: you read the drafts and press send yourself.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Finds (or on the first run creates) your Sheet and reads the **Leads** tab so companies you already have are skipped (matched by website domain).\n2. Apify `santamaria-automations/google-maps-scraper` returns 20 places for today's search × city pair. Places without a website, closed places and known domains are dropped; at most `newPerDay` are kept.\n3. Apify `santamaria-automations/website-contact-extractor` reads each website's contact pages (no API key needed). A role inbox (events@, hello@, info@ …) is picked; personal addresses are never used.\n4. Companies still without an inbox go to `santamaria-automations/website-email-scraper` (up to 5 pages per site).\n5. Every new company gets a row (status `to review`). Companies with an inbox also get a Gmail draft built from your template in **Settings**.\n\n**Setup (about 10 minutes)**\n1. Install the verified community node `@apify/n8n-nodes-apify` (tested with 0.9.0; install guide: https://docs.apify.com/platform/integrations/n8n). It works on n8n Cloud and self-hosted. Connect your Apify account in the three Apify nodes (OAuth2 on Cloud or an API token).\n2. Connect Google Sheets (Sheet and HTTP nodes) and Gmail. On the first run the workflow creates the Sheet **Daily outreach drafts - NanoScrape** in your Drive with a **Leads** tab and header row; later runs find it by name.\n3. Open **Settings**: your searches and cities (one per line; each weekday uses the next pair), how many new companies per day, your name, and the email subject/body. `{company}`, `{category}` and `{city}` are filled in per company.\n4. The Gmail node only **creates drafts**. Nothing is ever sent.\n5. Test with **Test workflow**, then activate. The trigger runs Monday to Friday at 6 AM (your n8n timezone).\n\n**Times:** dates in the Sheet and the 'every weekday' schedule use your n8n timezone (Settings → Timezone).\n\n**Tested on** n8n 2.35.7 and 2.47.7 (self-hosted), 2026-11-16.\n\n**Cost** (Apify Store prices, checked 2026-11-16): Maps $0.001 per place, contact extractor $0.01 per website with contacts, email scraper $0.001 per page, plus small start fees. 10 new companies a day ≈ $0.15-0.20 a day. The Maps search runs every day even when it finds 0 new companies (about $0.02 for 20 places), which is why Settings rotates through several searches and cities: the same search returns mostly the same places every day. Every Apify node has a **Max cost per run** cap.\n\n**Limits**\n- Drafts are a template, not AI-written. Personalise before you send.\n- Only inboxes published on the company's own website are used. No guessing, no SMTP verification.\n- Check your local rules for B2B email (for example GDPR/PECR) before sending.",
        "height": 1240,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
